steps.message:
The fitness-for-service assessment on file for T-01-002 records a measured thickness below the acceptance criterion applied. Assess the record as it stands at 06/15/2026 and establish what the record supports as the disposition of this tank. Carry each course 1 grid forward at its own rate to 06/15/2026.

Please author a new document file (`T01002_FFS_DISPOSITION.docx`) as a memo setting out what the assessment on file establishes, what it does not, and what you would do before the GPSOA submission. Give the records your conclusions rest on. Support the memo with tables and with the following appendices:

- Appendix A: the governing course readings on every basis the survey workbook records them, giving for each the grid reference, elevation, reading, baseline and date, and, on each basis the survey records, the minimum and the count of grids below the acceptance criterion both as surveyed and at 06/15/2026, together with the grid that crosses the acceptance criterion between those dates and the date on which it crosses;
- Appendix B: a check of the assessment on file against each input the site guidance requires to be recorded on the face of an assessment, giving for each whether it is recorded, the value and its source;
- Appendix C: the inputs a further assessment would need, giving for each the value, the record and its date where the record holds it, and identifying those the record does not hold;
- Appendix D: a dated chronology of the records bearing on the disposition up to 06/15/2026, including what the inspection plan on file for this tank schedules next.

Commit to one defensible disposition; do not present multiple branches or hedge between options.

Report thicknesses in inches (in), corrosion rates in mils per year (mpy) and remaining life in years (yr), and give all dates as MM/DD/YYYY. The governing basis is API 579-1 Part 4, API 653 and TC-MECH-PROC-0007 Rev 2. Round thicknesses to three decimal places, rates to two decimal places and remaining life to one decimal place. Produce output reflecting professional engineering standards.

The material sits in:

- `/Integrity/Tanks/T-01-002/`, holding the inspection report, the fitness-for-service assessment, the inspection plan and the process data sheet;
- `/Integrity/Tanks/T-01-001/`, holding the assessments on file for the neighboring asset;
- `/Integrity/Procedures/`, holding the site fitness-for-service assessment guidance;
- `/Integrity/Programme/`, holding the mechanical integrity written programme, the 2026 tank inspection programme, the fitness-for-service tracker and the corrosion rate and remaining life workbook;
- `/Integrity/Surveys/`, holding the 2025 contractor UT thickness survey workbooks.

